&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;13&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;14&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Attention to detail and an appreciation of time management&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;#LI-BC1&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You belong at Burson:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our vision is for Burson to be the leading ‘academy company’ for creative communications professionals and emerging leaders. We provide a dynamic environment where ambitious colleagues come to elevate their skills, expand their networks, and ultimately, produce the best solutions for today’s leading brands. Our commitment to your growth is reflected in our robust benefits and people programs, which include professional development opportunities, mentorship programs with industry leaders, a vibrant and inclusive company culture fostering collaboration and innovation and packages designed to reward and retain top talent. We invest in our people because we believe their success is our success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Burson, we’re an agency of learn-it-alls. We recognize that the things we do best, creativity and communications, require a level of nuanced understanding. That’s why it’s imperative for us to hire extraordinarily talented people of all backgrounds and identities. Without that we can’t do the essential work of inspiring bold ideas, fostering constructive dialogue, cultivating meaningful experiences, and driving innovation and creativity for our partners. Your unique point of view—your talent—is what makes you a #BursonPerson, and it’s how we deliver exceptional results for our clients, together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe the best work happens when we&#39;re together, fostering creativity, collaboration, and connection. That&#39;s why we’ve adopted a hybrid approach, with teams in the office around four days a week. If you require accommodations or flexibility, please discuss this with the hiring team during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When you click the &quot;Submit Application&quot; button below, this will send any information you add below to Burson. Before you do this, we think it&#39;s a good idea to read through our &amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bursonglobal.com/p/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy. &lt;/a&gt;California residents should read our  &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bursonglobal.com/p/california-recruitment-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;California Recruitment Privacy Notice. &lt;/a&gt;This explains what we do with your personal data when you apply for a role with us, and, how you can update the information you have provided us with or how to remove it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;font-display font-bold text-[19px] mt-5 mb-1.5&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed mb-2&quot;&gt;When a customer pushes a change, they need their CI/CD jobs to start quickly and run reliably, even when demand spikes. You&#39;ll help make that happen on GitLab.com by improving how Hosted Runners provision compute, isolate customer workloads, and recover from failures. Your decisions will shape how long customers wait for jobs to start and how efficiently GitLab uses cloud compute.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed mb-2&quot;&gt;As a Senior Staff Site Reliability Engineer, you&#39;ll set technical direction across teams while continuing to write and operate production software in Go. You&#39;ll lead work across the runner control plane, worker provisioning, and job execution. Your primary focus will be GitLab.com, and you&#39;ll also provide technical leadership support for GitLab Dedicated Hosted Runners. You&#39;ll report to the engineering manager responsible for Hosted Runners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;text-[15px] mb-1 font-semibold&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Some examples of our projects:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;space-y-1.5 ml-4&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Tuning autoscaling to reduce job wait times during demand spikes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Evaluating ways to isolate customer workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Improving how runner usage is measured for capacity planning and billing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;font-display font-bold text-[19px] mt-5 mb-1.5&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;space-y-1.5 ml-4&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Lead architecture and delivery across teams. Plan migrations with representative workload tests, safe capacity handovers, and rollback paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Write, review, and ship Go code across GitLab Runner, autoscaling components, cloud integrations, and operational tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Improve reliability from job pickup through cleanup. Join the Runners Platform on-call rotation, investigate failures across system layers, and verify fixes in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Work with Security and Runner engineers to evaluate workload isolation, balancing security and compatibility with performance and cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Build observability that connects the customer experience with fleet behavior and guides capacity decisions. Partner with Finance, Product, and the billing platform team on usage metering and cost attribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Reduce recurring operational work through automation, tooling, and runbooks that engineers can use independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Mentor experienced engineers through design, implementation, and operations. Clarify ownership across teams and help engineers validate AI-assisted changes before they reach production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;font-display font-bold text-[19px] mt-5 mb-1.5&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;space-y-1.5 ml-4&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Recent hands-on experience building and operating production systems software such as controllers, agents, or schedulers. You&#39;ve personally shipped code that handles challenges such as concurrency, retries, or resource cleanup.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Strong programming skills in Go or another systems language, with the ability to become productive in Go.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Deep Linux and networking knowledge. You can trace production failures across system layers and use measurements to validate fixes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Experience operating Kubernetes in production, including diagnosing scheduling and resource issues and managing rollouts and recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Experience building or operating autoscaled or dynamically scheduled compute, such as VM fleets, serverless platforms, or batch systems. You bring experience with public cloud and infrastructure automation or comparable fleet operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;A working understanding of the CI job lifecycle and the implications of running customer-controlled code. You can bring that knowledge from outside a CI/CD team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;A record of leading technical initiatives across teams and personally contributing to implementation through production. You build agreement through clear writing and asynchronous collaboration, and mentor engineers to own what they build and operate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;font-display font-bold text-[19px] mt-5 mb-1.5&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed mb-2&quot;&gt;Hosted Runners operates the compute behind customers&#39; CI/CD jobs. You&#39;ll work with Runner Core to turn lessons from operating the fleet into improvements to the open-source GitLab Runner. You&#39;ll also work with Product and partner teams to agree on priorities and ownership for shared changes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;text-[15px] mb-1 font-semibold&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn more:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ml-4 space-y-1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;text-[15px] font-medium&quot; href=&quot;https://docs.gitlab.com/administration/dedicated/hosted_runners/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Hosted runners for GitLab Dedicated (docs)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The base salary range for this role’s listed level is currently for residents of the&amp;nbsp;United States only. This range is intended to reflect the role&#39;s base salary rate in locations throughout the US.&amp;nbsp;Grade level and salary ranges are determined through interviews and a review of education, experience, knowledge, skills, abilities of the applicant, equity with other team members, alignment with market data,&amp;nbsp;and geographic location.&amp;nbsp;The base salary range does not include any bonuses, equity, or benefits. See more information on our &lt;a class=&quot;waffle-rich-text-link&quot; href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-link=&quot;https://bit.ly/GLBeneUS&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#1155cc;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:underline;font-family:&#39;&#39;Arial&#39;&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt;benefits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:none;font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;waffle-rich-text-link&quot; href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/stock-options/&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-link=&quot;https://bit.ly/GLequity&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#1155cc;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:underline;font-family:&#39;&#39;Arial&#39;&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt;equity&lt;/a&gt;. Sales roles are also eligible for incentive pay targeted at up to 100% of the offered base salary.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;United States Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$184,800&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$314,400 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Intermediate Backend Engineer in GitLab&#39;s Agent Foundations stage, you&#39;ll go beyond using AI tools. You&#39;ll help build the foundations for GitLab&#39;s agentic AI experiences: the platform that lets AI agents work across the whole software delivery lifecycle, not just write code. That covers how agents are created, shared and connected to tools inside and outside GitLab, how they run, and how their work shows up and can be observed across GitLab.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you&#39;ll work closely with engineers across the stage and other AI Engineering teams. This is a high-visibility area where GitLab&#39;s core platform meets its AI strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, ship and maintain features for the Duo Agent Platform in the GitLab monolith (Ruby) and, where needed, the AI Gateway (Python). Keep them secure, well-tested and performant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product Management, UX, frontend, backend and AI specialists to refine requirements and ship improvements in small iterations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement and review GraphQL and REST APIs and the backend logic behind them, with reliable, scalable and clear contracts for clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve and extend automated testing (RSpec and other frameworks) to strengthen quality and give developers faster feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share standards, patterns and learnings with other engineers to raise the bar for responsible AI integration and evidence-driven engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Join Tier 2 &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/engineering/infrastructure-platforms/incident-management/on-call/tier-2/&quot;&gt;on-call rotations&lt;/a&gt; to troubleshoot production issues, contribute to root cause analysis, and improve observability and resiliency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep an eye on the competitive landscape to help keep GitLab&#39;s agent platform best-in-class.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and maintaining production Ruby on Rails applications, including background jobs, APIs and data models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working across the stack in a mature codebase. Familiarity with Python backends and/or Vue frontends is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skill in designing or extending REST and/or GraphQL APIs with attention to scalability, maintainability and backward compatibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real enthusiasm for AI and hands-on experience using AI tools in your daily work. Experience designing and shipping AI-powered backend features or integrations is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven SQL and experience with relational databases such as PostgreSQL, including writing efficient queries and data modeling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience finding and fixing performance bottlenecks in applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication, including technical proposals and documentation, in a remote, async, cross-functional team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Openness to learning and to applying skills from related technologies or fields.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/engineering/ai/agent-foundations/&quot;&gt;Agent Foundations stage&lt;/a&gt; builds the foundations for GitLab&#39;s agentic AI experiences. We provide the platform, catalog and execution features that help teams deliver resilient agents and flows to customers. The stage has three groups: Agent Developer, AI Catalog and Agent Execution, they provide the core harness for GitLab’s agents, the tools Agent’s need to interact with GitLab as well as ways to configure and execute Agents across GitLab.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our engineers work async-first across EMEA and AMER timezones. We work with teams across AI engineering and the rest of GitLab so the Duo Agent Platform can power many of GitLab&#39;s AI features.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every change to Anthropic&#39;s software has to reach production somehow: new code, runtime configuration, feature flags, infrastructure changes. Our team builds the systems those changes travel through. Our mission is to give every team at Anthropic a fast, safe, and predictable path from change to production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join the team within Anthropic&#39;s Infrastructure organization that owns pipelines, staged rollouts, health-gated promotion, and rollback, along with runtime configuration, feature flags, and the systems that deliver code and artifacts to machines across a very large fleet. You&#39;ll own a meaningful part of this end to end, from design through operating it in production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want your work to shape how fast and how safely Anthropic ships, this could be a great fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set technical direction for major parts of the deployment platform and own them end to end: design, implementation, operations, and on-call&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build rollout safety into the platform, including progressive delivery, health-gated promotion, automatic pause and rollback, and deploy controls that teams manage themselves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design APIs and abstractions that work equally well for engineers and for AI agents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extend the platform to new workload types and runtimes, from Kubernetes to serverless and edge platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and operate runtime configuration and feature flag systems with validation, gradual rollout, and fast rollback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build infrastructure-as-code workflows that many teams rely on for safe, routine changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale artifact distribution so code and configuration reach machines quickly and efficiently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Security so that the path to production is secure by default, with verifiable builds, least-privilege access, and auditable changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with teams across Anthropic to understand their deployment needs and bring their workloads onto the platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take part in on-call and incident response, and turn what you learn into guardrails so the same problem can&#39;t recur&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in at least one backend or systems programming language, such as Rust, Go, C++, or Java&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading the design, building, and operation of distributed systems or infrastructure in production, including technical direction across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud infrastructure and containerized workloads, such as Kubernetes on AWS or GCP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building deployment, release, or change management systems at large scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with production on-call and incident response&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Rust in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with progressive delivery and GitOps tooling, such as Argo CD or Argo Rollouts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of Kubernetes, including controllers and operators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Terraform or other infrastructure-as-code systems at scale, including state management and locking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building feature flag, experimentation, or dynamic configuration systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with artifact or package distribution, such as OCI registries, Nix, or content-addressed storage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with software supply chain security, such as signed build provenance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building high-throughput workflow engines or control planes backed by relational databases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building internal developer platforms and driving adoption across many teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI agents in your own engineering work, or building systems that agents operate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Representative projects&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build operator controls for progressive rollouts, including pause and resume that preserve rollout state&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design a deployment engine built on fine-grained targets and their dependencies, so each change rolls out exactly where it needs to&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build cluster-health-aware rollouts that steer around unhealthy clusters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add a new workload type to the platform, including its rollout, verification, and rollback behavior&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design a deployment control plane that handles sharp bursts of agent-driven traffic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design a distribution system that delivers configuration and artifacts to every machine in the fleet as demand grows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£325,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£390,000 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum education: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required field of study:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum years of experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location-based hybrid policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren&#39;t able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For roles performing work in California: &lt;/strong&gt;We will consider for employment all qualified applicants, including those with arrest or conviction records or criminal histories, in a manner consistent with the requirements of applicable state and local laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the City of Los Angeles’ Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.&lt;/strong&gt; Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&amp;nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you&#39;re interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we&#39;re building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Your safety matters to us.&lt;/strong&gt; To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you ----- addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you&#39;re ever unsure about a communication, don&#39;t click any links—visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u data-stringify-type=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-remove-tab-index=&quot;true&quot;&gt;anthropic.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;re different&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We&#39;re an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp;amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team builds, tests, deploys, and monitors the classifiers that block internal agents from taking dangerous actions. These classifiers run across RL, evals, and internal deployments, and are designed to catch things like sandbox escape attempts or exfiltration of sensitive data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When a classifier flags an action, it can &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/news/improving-alignment-security-efforts&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;block the action before the tool call runs, end the task, and alert a human&lt;/a&gt;. This is one layer of a defence-in-depth with several layers that reinforce each other: what our classifiers flag feeds into offline monitoring, and the findings from that go back into better classifiers and safer environment design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The work combines research and production engineering:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The research problem is building high recall and high precision classifiers to catch rare, novel, and sometimes adversarial behaviour. There are also several narrow research questions to answer - for example, how to deploy safety classifiers inside training environments without incentivising models to evade them. Some research also builds on the multi-stage designs described in our work on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/claude-code-auto-mode&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Claude Code auto mode&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/research/next-generation-constitutional-classifiers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Constitutional Classifiers&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The engineering problem is shipping these classifiers into the critical path of research and product work. These classifiers need to cover a huge volume of traffic while operating within cost, latency and availability constraints.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Day to day, much of our work is done with Claude: you&#39;ll direct agents to run experiments and ship code, and review what they produce. That moves the hard part of the job towards deciding what to do and in what order. Additionally, organisation, communication, and prioritisation skills matter a great deal as our classifiers sit in the path of many other teams&#39; work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Design, train, and evaluate classifiers that detect unsafe agent actions in real time, owning pieces such as prompted models, trained classifiers, or probes on model internals&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deploy, tune and operate these classifiers in the critical path of internal agents, RL training, and evaluations, and own their accuracy, reliability, latency, cost, and failure behaviour&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build the datasets, labelling pipelines, and evaluations that allow us to measure and improve our classifiers and harm taxonomies&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with red teaming colleagues to stress-test our classifiers, and harden them against what they find&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work with the teams whose agents, environments, and evaluations we run on, so that false positives get fixed quickly without weakening protection&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contribute to the team&#39;s direction, including what to build, what to partner on, and where to invest&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to organise and prioritise several parallel streams of work, and to communicate clearly with the teams that work affects&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to critically review code and experiment results, including work produced by AI agents&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sincere interest in developing safe and beneficial AI systems&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience leading ambiguous technical projects and setting direction for other engineers or researchers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience evaluating large language models, developing classifiers, or operating high-scale production systems where requirements change quickly&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience building detection systems where true positives are rare and false positives are costly, such as abuse, fraud, spam, or intrusion detection&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience running low-latency, high-availability services that other systems depend on, including being on call for them&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience fine-tuning language models, or working with probes and other methods that read model internals&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with LLM inference or serving infrastructure, or with integrating new components into training infrastructure&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Background in security, such as sandboxing or detection and response&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with research on AI control, scalable oversight, agent safety, or reinforcement learning&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
